# openrouter-mullvad-proxy-refused

- **Timestamp:** 2026-07-29T09:44+03:30
- **Host:** t3-new (`ssh t3 -p 80`; port 22 timed out)

## Symptom

```
openrouter request: Post "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions":
proxyconnect tcp: dial tcp 172.19.0.4:8778: connect: connection refused
```

`lexmora-api` env: `OPENROUTER_HTTP_PROXY=http://mullvad-1:8778`  
`mullvad-1` on `openvpn-net` = `172.19.0.4`

## Findings

| Component | Status |
|-----------|--------|
| Mullvad VPN (`mullvad-1`) | **OK** — Connected, relay `de-dus-wg-003`, exit `185.254.75.50` (Germany) |
| HTTP proxy (`openrouter-proxy` / 3proxy `:8778`) | **DOWN** — Exited (127) ~10h ago |
| Port 8778 | Not listening on host or inside `mullvad-1` |

Root cause: `openrouter-proxy` used `--network container:<old-mullvad-id>`. After Mullvad was recreated, join failed:

```
joining network namespace of container: No such container: 522f9b01af6e...
```

Current `mullvad-1` id: `e0f0a561dbe2...` (started ~05:03 UTC).

## Fix (applied 2026-07-29)

1. Manual recreate (immediate), then made permanent:

### Compose (survives `./openvpn.sh` / mullvad recreate)

Added `openrouter-proxy` to `/home/cloud-admin/irancell-t3/docker/composes/openvpn/openvpn.yml` with the same SoftEther pattern:

- `network_mode: "service:mullvad-1"`
- `depends_on: [mullvad-1]`
- `restart: unless-stopped`
- volumes under `/cloud-admin/docker-volumes/openvpn/openrouter-proxy/`

`openvpn.sh` creates proxy dirs and calls `ensure-openrouter-proxy.sh` after `compose up`.

### Systemd (survives host reboot)

- Unit: `openrouter-proxy.service` (enabled)
- Script: `/home/cloud-admin/irancell-t3/docker/deploy/ensure-openrouter-proxy.sh`
- Installer: `.../docker/deploy/install-openrouter-proxy-systemd.sh`

### Verification

- Compose project `openvpn`, service `openrouter-proxy`
- `:8778` listening; OpenRouter via proxy HTTP 200
- `systemctl is-enabled openrouter-proxy.service` → enabled
